<b>יב.</b> Without an aim - but if the increaser aimed as well, the increaser is better. And if the one who diminishes has rape and is unable to prolong it, or if he imagines in himself that if he prolongs it - he will not be able to repent, and if he diminishes in supplications and says them on purpose, he is considered before the blessed Hashem as one who has leisure and prolongs his supplications on purpose. And on this we both: "One who increases and one who decreases, provided that their hearts are toward heaven." And in the matter of Talmud Torah, the matter is yes, because everything depends before Hashem, may Hashem bless him, if he does everything he has the power to do. And he who is a Torah scholar and has a heart to understand and learn, can avoid saying many supplications and requests that are printed in siddurs, and it is better for him to learn instead. And a person should set a time for him to study moral books every day, whether a little or a lot, because the greatest of his creation is the greatest of ours. And the spice of the evil inclination is the rebuke of the articles of the Sages.
